AI generated proposal to improve performance for @pullfrog to evaluate:

Every schema instance allocates its own Set for _zod.traits, and V8 charges a flat 224 B for one regardless of size. The trait chain is fixed by the constructor, not the instance, so $constructor keeps the first instance's set and points later instances at it — compared with sameMembers rather than assumed, so a differing chain falls back to its own set.

Impact: −14.0% retained memory on a realistic schema catalogue (z.string() −29.6%, z.object() 10 keys −23.2%). Parse unchanged. Construction +4% on leaf schemas, −5.8% on discriminated unions. Bundle +47 B gzip classic, +68 B mini.

