## Real-world Context
This issue occurs in a production codebase where we're migrating from Zod v3 to v4. The schemas represent complex business domain relationships that naturally have many circular dependencies. While we can potentially restructure the schemas, it would be valuable to understand the recommended approach for such cases.

Any guidance on handling complex circular schema networks in Zod v4 would be greatly appreciated!

We have a number of nominal/branded types, one such example being seconds. In certain contexts the maximum value of seconds in 60, in other situations it might be 3600, in others it may have no bounding at all. It would be useful to be able to define a shared nominal types then refine it further where necessary depending on the context.

```
const secondsSchema = z.number().describe('...').brand<Seconds>();
const minuteSecondsSchema = secondsSchema.min(0).max(60);
const hourSecondsSchema = secondsSchema.min(0).max(3600);
```

As it stands you need to duplicate the base schema every time for every variant of the same thing.

