Currently Zod only supports character-based length validation for strings (`max()`, `min()`, `.length()`) but there's no way to validate word count.

### Current Workaround

```ts
const schema = z.object({
  about: z
    .string()
    .refine(
      (val) => {
        if (!val || val.trim() === "") return true;
        const words = val
          .trim()
          .split(/\s+/)
          .filter((word) => word.length > 0);
        return words.length <= 200; // max 200 words
      },
      {
        message: "About section must be less than 200 words",
      }
    )
});
```

### Proposed Solution

```ts
z.string().words({ max: 200 }) // max 200 words
z.string().words({ min: 10, max: 200 }) // max 200 words, min 10 words
z.string().words({ exact: 100 }) // exactly 100 words
```

