Trying to upgrade codebase to zod 4, and came across an issue with extending a schema with defaults. 
We have been using this pattern with zod 3 (3.25.x):

```ts
const base = z.object({
  foo: z.string().default('foobar')
})

const extended = base.partial().extend({
  bar: z.string().optional()
});

// Zod 3 does not apply the default value
console.log(extended.parse({})); // {}
```

With Zod 4:

```ts
const base = z.object({
  foo: z.string().default('foobar')
})

const extended = z.object({
  ...base.partial().shape,
  bar: z.string().optional()
})

// 💣 Zod 4 applies default value here
console.log(extended.parse({})) // -> {foo: "foobar"}
```

In zod 4 the defaults are applied to the extended schema, which imo makes more sense.
